{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0190"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c016): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c016.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0190"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/physical","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__physical.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1022],["+","Island nations have smaller champions. Biwa, Inawashiro and Kasumigaura are lakes in Japan, among the largest of that mountainous country. Lake Biwa, north-east of Kyoto, covers about 670 square kilometres and formed some four million years ago, which makes it one of the oldest lakes on Earth; it supplies drinking water to more than ten million people in Kyoto and Osaka. Kasumigaura, a shallow lagoon north-east of Tokyo, is the country's second largest, and Inawashiro lies at the foot of the volcano Bandai in Fukushima Prefecture.\n\n"],["=",213]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",956],["+","Inselstaaten haben kleinere Spitzenreiter. Biwa, Inawashiro und Kasumigaura sind Seen in Japan, und sie gehören zu den größten des gebirgigen Landes. Der Biwa-See nordöstlich von Kyōto bedeckt etwa 670 Quadratkilometer und entstand vor rund vier Millionen Jahren, was ihn zu einem der ältesten Seen der Erde macht; er versorgt mehr als zehn Millionen Menschen in Kyōto und Osaka mit Trinkwasser. Der Kasumigaura, eine flache Lagune nordöstlich von Tokio, ist der zweitgrößte des Landes, und der Inawashiro liegt am Fuß des Vulkans Bandai in der Präfektur Fukushima.\n\n"],["=",197]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0190"},"reason":"a0190 bodyDe: \"In Nordamerika bedeckt der Obere See, …\" → \"Nordamerikas Riese heißt Oberer See: Der westlichste der Großen Seen … bedeckt …\" — f00950's DE span was in the closing paragraph; the sentence now holds the nominative answer — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Superior","by":"enrich batch 080","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0010-a0502.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Superior"}]},
